after years of waiting the batman has  finally swooped into theaters it's been  a long road for this new version of the  dark knight to make its way to the big  screen as a production was hit with  pandemic-related delays and setbacks  robert pattinson himself reportedly  caught covert 19 during filming so it's  a minor miracle that warner brothers has  finally been able to release the matt  reeves directed movie thankfully the  film pushes its cast of dc heroes and  villains in new directions many of which  should even surprise longtime fans the  action kicks off in bruce wayne's second  year of crime fighting so audiences  don't have to sit through yet another  origin story when a sadistic individual  called the riddler starts targeting the  corrupt officials of gotham batman sets  out to stop his violent war before the  villain can hurt the rest of the city  the caped crusader also crosses paths  with some other iconic characters from  the batman mythos as he gets help from  lieutenant james gordon and catwoman aka  selena kyle he even goes up against two  other iconic bad villains penguin and  carmine falcone who are at the heart of  organized crime in gotham that said  there's never any doubt to the big bad  of this film is when it comes to the  film's cryptics you're your killer  director matt reeves and co-writer peter  craig take a new approach to the riddle  obsessed villain before we go any  further be warned spoilers ahead let's  get the most obvious change out of the  way first the riddler's new duds gone  are the days of bright green spandex  with question marks painted all over  no this version of the villain takes a  more tactical approach to his look he  sports a dark green military jacket with  a similarly coloured hoodie underneath  then there's his incredibly creepy mask  that he wears with transparent glasses  over the top to mask his real identity  which we'll get to later on after the  first teaser for the film arrived back  in august 2020 comics writer nick  darrington took to twitter to point out  that riddler's headgear is actually an  extreme cold weather mask used by the  u.s military so why does riddler take a  diy approach to his terrifying look well  for starters he doesn't have the same  funds as bruce wayne to create a  high-tech suit so he probably shops in  army surplus stores for his gear let's  not forget that this version of the  villain is much more of a homegrown  terrorist than jim carrey's gleeful  mischief maker in batman forever he's  also a huge departure from the sharp  suited version of the character in the  gotham tv series the small screen's  riddler is also a former gcpd forensic  scientist although he clearly enjoys  taunting gotham in his live streams a  flamboyant eccentric riddler wouldn't  fit into this universe that matt reeves  is building the riddler also tells the  hero that his mask allows him to become  his true self it's all an attempt to  bond with batman as he points out that  the caped crusaders persona is also his  true face it's the classic with the same  you and i approach to connecting the  hero and the villain there's another  surprising difference in the riddler's  character from what dc fans might expect  his name isn't edward nigma this time  around the villain uses his birth name  edward nashton a choice that's mainly  about making sure these characters feel  natural to the world of the batman the  enigma joke wouldn't work as well here  it just feels kind of silly sure  nashton's job as an accountant is a real  reason behind his roaring corruption in  the first place but the riddler persona  is who he really is plus he's already  projecting majorly enigmatic vibes even  without the pseudonym when the police  eventually managed to arrest the riddler  his wallet is filled with a couple of id  cards so they're not 100 sure who he  actually is riddler's detached  personality his unhinged crimes and his  bizarre costume even called back to a  real life serial killer when speaking to  movie maker reef said the premise of the  movie is that the riddler is kind of  moulded in an almost zodiac killer sort  of mode it's easy to see the connection  since a riddler sends messages written  in code much like the zodiac killer who  terrified san francisco in the 1970s  thankfully alfred pennyworth happens to  be a master code breaker which is hugely  helpful when he and bruce are picking  apart with those cryptic messages  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite dc movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

